{
  "book": "Song of Solomon",
  "commentary": "Darby Translation Notes",
  "author": "John Nelson Darby",
  "entries": [
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 1,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 1,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Solomon's. (a-7) The separate paragraphs indicate, as far as possible, the succession of the various speakers."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 2,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 2,
      "title": "",
      "content": "love (b-13) Heb. 'loves.' so ver. 4; chs. 4.10; 7.12. It is the same word as that used in the singular for the 'beloved,' ver. 13, &c., whence also the name David."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 4,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 4,
      "title": "",
      "content": "remember (c-28) Or 'celebrate.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 6,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 6,
      "title": "",
      "content": "me. (d-15) Or 'hath burned me.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 7,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 7,
      "title": "",
      "content": "veiled (e-28) Others, 'roving.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 9,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 9,
      "title": "",
      "content": "love, (f-5) Or 'friend.' it is feminine and occurs in ver. 15; chs. 2.2,10,13; 4.1,7; 5.2; 6.4. (It is not the same as chs. 2.7; 3.5; 7.6; 8.4.) This feminine form of the word is only found in this Book and Judg. 11.37,38, and Ps. 45.14. The masculine form 'friend' occurs in ch. 5.1,16; 2Sam. 15.37; 16.16, &c."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 13,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 13,
      "title": "",
      "content": "night (g-14) Or 'That passeth the night,' or 'abideth.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 1,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 1,
      "title": "",
      "content": "narcissus (a-4) Feminine, as Isa. 35.1. Sharon, (b-6) See 1Chron. 27.29."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 7,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 7,
      "title": "",
      "content": "charge (c-2) Or 'adjure,' and so chs. 3.5; 5.8,9; 8.4. please. (d-28) Lit. 'nor awaken love till it please.' so chs. 3.5 and 8.4."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 9,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 9,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Glancing (e-23) Or 'showing himself.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 17,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 17,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Turn, (f-10) Or 'Return.' Bether. (g-26) Meaning, cloven, or full of ravines."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 3,
      "start_verse": 5,
      "end_chapter": 3,
      "end_verse": 5,
      "title": "",
      "content": "you, (a-3) See ch. 2.7."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 3,
      "start_verse": 10,
      "end_chapter": 3,
      "end_verse": 10,
      "title": "",
      "content": "support (b-8) Or 'bottom part.' By (c-22) Or 'from.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 4,
      "start_verse": 3,
      "end_chapter": 4,
      "end_verse": 3,
      "title": "",
      "content": "temples (d-22) Or 'cheeks;' and so ch. 6.7."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 4,
      "start_verse": 8,
      "end_chapter": 4,
      "end_verse": 8,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Amanah, (a-19) * Said to mean 'firmness' or 'constancy.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 4,
      "start_verse": 14,
      "end_chapter": 4,
      "end_verse": 14,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Calamus (b-4) As 'sweet cane;' Jer. 6.20."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 5,
      "start_verse": 8,
      "end_chapter": 5,
      "end_verse": 8,
      "title": "",
      "content": "charge (a-2) Or 'adjure.' and so in ver. 9; ch. 8.4; see also ch. 2.7."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 5,
      "start_verse": 10,
      "end_chapter": 5,
      "end_verse": 10,
      "title": "",
      "content": "chiefest (b-8) Strictly, 'lifted up as a banner.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 5,
      "start_verse": 14,
      "end_chapter": 5,
      "end_verse": 14,
      "title": "",
      "content": "bright (c-12) Or 'wrought-work of.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 6,
      "start_verse": 12,
      "end_chapter": 6,
      "end_verse": 12,
      "title": "",
      "content": "people. (a-15) Singular of Ammim. see Ps. 7.8; 'willing,' is as Ps. 47.9. see Ps. 110.3."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 6,
      "start_verse": 13,
      "end_chapter": 6,
      "end_verse": 13,
      "title": "",
      "content": "camps. (b-30) As Gen. 32.2."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 7,
      "start_verse": 9,
      "end_chapter": 7,
      "end_verse": 9,
      "title": "",
      "content": "... (c-11) The feminine speaker interrupts here. for (d-16) Or 'that floweth straight to.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 7,
      "start_verse": 13,
      "end_chapter": 7,
      "end_verse": 13,
      "title": "",
      "content": "mandrakes (e-2) Gen. 30.14."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 8,
      "start_verse": 2,
      "end_chapter": 8,
      "end_verse": 2,
      "title": "",
      "content": "wouldest (f-12) Or 'She would.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 8,
      "start_verse": 4,
      "end_chapter": 8,
      "end_verse": 4,
      "title": "",
      "content": "please? (a-19) See chs. 2.7; 3.5."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 8,
      "start_verse": 11,
      "end_chapter": 8,
      "end_verse": 11,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Baal-hamon. (b-6) Meaning, 'Master of a multitude.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 8,
      "start_verse": 14,
      "end_chapter": 8,
      "end_verse": 14,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Haste (c-1) Lit. 'Break away.'"
    }
  ]
}
